From ae1ef6a97607d4d11749a972481a6dfa1d75fb2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:42:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HIP/RDNA3 MMQ: Q4_K/Q5_K scale epilogue in VOPD-pairable f32
 ops, bitwise the same sums (GGML_HIP_MMQ_EPI=0 off)

Per k01 step of the Q4_K J=128 prefill tile, ggml_cuda_mmq_vec_dot_q8_1_q8_1_mma ran 16 v_wmma_i32_16x16x16_iu8
against 64 v_cvt_f32_i32 + 128 v_fma_mix_f32 + 64 fmac (237 VALU instructions): the scale products used v_fma_mix
(the f16->f32 conversions folded in) and the accumulators v_cvt_f32_i32, neither of which can dual-issue (VOPD).
The epi variant of that vec_dot (RDNA3 only):
- widens the 8 x and the J/16 y half2 scales of a k01 step to f32 once (32 v_cvt_f32_f16; the x scales are shared by
  all y minitiles), hidden behind an empty asm (otherwise they fold back into v_fma_mix) in runs of 4 consecutive
  VGPRs, so that the scale products find different register banks for VOPD pairs;
- starts the int32 WMMA accumulator at 0x4B400000 instead of 0 and recovers (float) C with one v_add_f32 of
  -12582912 (VOPD) instead of v_cvt_f32_i32.
The k01 loop keeps the old non-unrolled shape (#pragma unroll 1: a full unroll made J=64 spill).

Bitwise: every output keeps the same IEEE operations in the same order.
- f16->f32 is exact and the product of two f16 values is exact in f32 (11+11 significand bits, |a*b| in
  [2^-48, 2^32]), so v_mul_f32(a.x, b.x) == v_fma_mix(a.x, b.x, -0) (signed zeros too) and
  v_fmac_f32(sum, a.y, b.y) == v_fma_mix(a.y, b.y, sum) (one rounding of a.y*b.y + sum in both); both kernels run
  with f16 and f32 denormals preserved (amdhsa_float_denorm_mode 3/3).
- |C| <= 32*128*128 = 2^19 < 2^22: the WMMA integer sum is exact with either start value (no saturation), the bits
  0x4B400000 + C are the float 12582912 + C, and the subtraction gives exactly C (+0 for C == 0) like v_cvt_f32_i32.
- sum = fma(scale product, C, sum) is the same v_fmac_f32; the k01 / tile / element order is unchanged.

Only the J >= 48 kernels without the row fallback (nrows % 128 == 0) take the variant: J=16 gets more instructions
(the widened x scales serve a single tile), J=32 the same, and the Q5_K J=128 fallback kernel would spill 13 VGPRs.
The switch selects kernel instantiations (template parameter), so GGML_HIP_MMQ_EPI=0 runs the old kernels: their
ISA is identical to c36fd2c87 (all 64 Q4_K and 64 Q5_K mul_mat_q/fixup bodies and VGPR counts compared).

Offline ISA (gfx1100, ROCm 10.0 clang, flags of the build):
- Q4_K J=128 inner k01 loop: 298 -> 243 instructions, VALU 237 -> 178 (126 VOPD); VGPRs 239 -> 240, no spills;
  J=96 VALU 182 -> 142 (190 -> 191 VGPRs), J=64 126 -> 105 (143 -> 147), J=48 100 -> 88 (123 -> 126).
- Q5_K J=128 VALU 239 -> 181 (244 -> 245 VGPRs), J=96 186 -> 141, J=64 127 -> 107, J=48 99 -> 88; no spills.
- LDS unchanged (Q4_K J=128: 38400 B, 3 blocks per WGP), so the occupancy stays LDS-bound at 3 blocks per WGP.

test-backend-ops: Q4_K/Q5_K MUL_MAT with 8192 rows and n = 48, 64, 96, 128, 512 (J = 48, 64, 96, 128) and a
MUL_MAT_ID case with 64 tokens per expert (J = 64) cover the variant.

UNMEASURED (no GPU access): pending test-backend-ops, bitwise logits A/B (hash and perplexity KLD) and llama-bench
pp512/pp4096 A/B.
